-- Same distribution and truncation as observeTwoSidedInterval, but spelled with
-- the `&&` connective the nested-if version exists to work around (see the
-- nested-if file's own comment): task set-witness-boolean-connectives gives
-- `invertToWorlds` cases for `and`/`or`/`not`, so the natural surface syntax
-- for a two-sided truncation now compiles too, and must agree value-for-value
-- with its nested-if twin.
main = let v = Normal in if (v > 0.0) && (v < 1.0) then right v else left ()
